# Vercel Speed Insights Installation Report

## Summary
Successfully installed and configured Vercel Speed Insights for the Next.js project following the latest official documentation from Vercel.

## Changes Implemented

### 1. Package Installation
- Installed `@vercel/speed-insights` package (version added to dependencies)
- Updated `package.json` with the new dependency
- Updated `package-lock.json` with resolved package versions

### 2. Code Configuration
**Modified: `src/app/layout.tsx`**
- Added import statement: `import { SpeedInsights } from "@vercel/speed-insights/next";`
- Added `<SpeedInsights />` component inside the `<body>` tag after the ToastProvider
- Placement follows the official Next.js App Router best practices

## Implementation Details

### Documentation Source
Fetched the latest installation instructions from: https://vercel.com/docs/speed-insights/quickstart

### Framework Detection
- Framework: Next.js 16.3.4 (App Router)
- Package Manager: npm
- TypeScript: Enabled

### Integration Approach
The SpeedInsights component was added to the root layout (`app/layout.tsx`) to ensure it runs on all pages. This is the recommended approach for Next.js App Router applications according to the official documentation.

